      "canonicalTargetId": "essential:enzyme",
      "surface": "enzymes",
      "startUtf16": 2984,
      "endUtf16": 2991,
      "quote": "DNA's instructions are used to make proteins in a two-step process. First, enzymes read the information in a DNA molecule and transcribe it into an intermediary molecule called messenger ribonucleic acid, or mRNA.",
